1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:02,040
Léa: Hello everyone and welcome

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:03,600
to The Cozy French!

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,780
I'm Léa.

4
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:06,200
Mathieu: And I'm Mathieu.

5
00:00:06,200 --> 00:00:08,460
Thank you for spending this time with us.

6
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:11,360
Get comfortable, wherever you are.

7
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:12,750
Léa: In your kitchen,

8
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:15,480
on the metro or during a little break,

9
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,920
you're very welcome.

10
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,940
Mathieu: Today, we're talking about food and nutrition.

11
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:23,810
So yes, I agreed to prepare

12
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:27,180
this episode with a lot of enthusiasm.

13
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:29,480
Léa: You even brought a file.

14
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:31,820
Mathieu: It's my quiche's CV.

15
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:34,940
It's looking for a place in your eating habits.

16
00:00:34,940 --> 00:00:36,840
Léa: Its main skills?

17
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:40,600
Mathieu: Bringing colleagues together around the table

18
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:43,840
and disappearing before the end of the break.

19
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:48,040
Léa: This conversation is for B1 and B2 levels.

20
00:00:48,040 --> 00:00:50,240
We're going to speak slowly, with

21
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:52,720
situations from everyday life.

22
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:53,350
Mathieu: By the end,

23
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:56,380
you'll be able to describe your eating habits

24
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:59,240
and ask questions about ingredients.

25
00:00:59,290 --> 00:01:02,200
Léa: You'll also be able to explain a small change

26
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,640
you'd like to make in your daily life.

27
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:08,080
Mathieu: No need to know all the names of vitamins.

28
00:01:08,080 --> 00:01:10,960
Me, I mostly know the names of cheeses.

29
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,800
Léa: We're going to talk about our meals,

30
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:16,680
a few nutrients and the pressure we sometimes feel.

31
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:19,680
Mathieu: Because choosing your lunch shouldn't

32
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:22,840
require a two-hour meeting.

33
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:26,240
Léa: If you don't understand every word, keep listening.

34
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,080
The context will help you.

35
00:01:28,130 --> 00:01:30,880
Mathieu: And you can repeat a sentence you like.

36
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:35,320
Your pronunciation can improve while your coffee cools down.

37
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:39,800
Léa: To start, think of a dish you often make.

38
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,120
What's in it?

39
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,040
Mathieu: And why do you like it?

40
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,040
Its taste?

41
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:45,240
Its price?

42
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:47,160
The memories it brings back?

43
00:01:47,160 --> 00:01:48,720
Léa: Keep your answer.

44
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:51,080
We'll help you tell it in French.

45
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:54,960
Mathieu: You can also tell us where you're listening from.

46
00:01:55,010 --> 00:01:58,600
I'm curious to know the dishes from your neighbourhood.

47
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:02,280
Léa: Last Saturday, I went to the market around 10.

48
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:04,220
It was chilly and the stallholders

49
00:02:04,220 --> 00:02:06,760
were still setting out their last baskets.

50
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,160
Mathieu: Did you have a list?

51
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:12,520
Léa: A small list, but a very big ambition.

52
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:16,040
I wanted to get back to a balanced diet

53
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,560
after several weeks of improvised meals.

54
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:23,060
Mathieu: A balanced diet, what does that mean in practice?

55
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:25,240
Léa: It's a way of eating varied food,

56
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:28,920
with different foods and amounts suited to your needs.

57
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:33,040
Mathieu: For example, my sister tries to keep a balanced

58
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:36,320
diet even when she travels for work.

59
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:39,810
Léa: Exactly. At the market, I bought carrots,

60
00:02:39,810 --> 00:02:42,480
a cabbage, leeks and apples.

61
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:45,280
Then a magnificent squash.

62
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,880
Mathieu: Magnificent how?

63
00:02:46,880 --> 00:02:48,320
Big enough to have its

64
00:02:48,320 --> 00:02:50,000
own seat on the bus?

65
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:52,670
Léa: Almost. On the way home, I had to carry it

66
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:55,600
against me like a little sleeping animal.

67
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:58,080
Mathieu: And had you planned to cook all that?

68
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:03,040
Léa: Yes, except that on Wednesday evening, the leeks were still waiting.

69
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,200
My eyes had been bigger than my stomach.

70
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,840
Mathieu: You'd bought more than you could eat?

71
00:03:07,840 --> 00:03:10,950
Léa: That's it. This expression means you want more

72
00:03:10,950 --> 00:03:13,320
food than you can actually eat.

73
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:14,730
Mathieu: At the hotel buffet,

74
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:17,440
my eyes were bigger than my stomach.

75
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:19,880
Three plates was too much.

76
00:03:19,930 --> 00:03:22,710
Léa: For me, the problem was also time.

77
00:03:22,710 --> 00:03:24,880
I'd forgotten my Monday meeting

78
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:26,400
and my Tuesday class.

79
00:03:26,400 --> 00:03:28,070
Mathieu: Your basket had a calmer

80
00:03:28,070 --> 00:03:30,040
schedule than you.

81
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:31,640
Léa: Much calmer.

82
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:34,800
So I made a soup for several meals.

83
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,040
And I froze some of the vegetables.

84
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:39,640
Mathieu: Did the whole basket find a destination?

85
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,840
Léa: Yes. But next week,

86
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,760
I'm going to ring the changes with

87
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,360
fewer things at a time.

88
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:47,120
Mathieu: Ring the changes?

89
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:48,710
Léa: Changing what you do or what

90
00:03:48,710 --> 00:03:51,280
you choose, to keep the pleasure.

91
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,960
Mathieu: To ring the changes,

92
00:03:52,960 --> 00:03:57,480
my neighbour picks a different walking route every Sunday.

93
00:03:57,480 --> 00:03:59,160
Léa: That's it. For meals,

94
00:03:59,160 --> 00:04:01,000
I can keep a simple base

95
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:04,000
and change the vegetables or the seasoning.

96
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,870
Mathieu: So you don't reinvent

97
00:04:05,870 --> 00:04:08,240
your whole kitchen every evening?

98
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:11,920
Léa: No. And a frozen vegetable can help me too.

99
00:04:11,920 --> 00:04:13,440
I don't need another

100
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:15,800
trip to the market to make every dinner.

101
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:20,200
Mathieu: The squash can finally take a few days off.

102
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:23,320
Me, on Friday, I made a mushroom

103
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:26,920
quiche for a shared lunch at the office.

104
00:04:26,920 --> 00:04:29,000
Léa: You really made it yourself?

105
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,870
Mathieu: Yes. My sister gave me her recipe.

106
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:34,640
This time, I got my hands dirty.

107
00:04:34,640 --> 00:04:37,180
Léa: You took part in the preparation.

108
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:39,490
That's the meaning of this expression,

109
00:04:39,490 --> 00:04:41,240
even when you're not cooking.

110
00:04:41,290 --> 00:04:43,620
Mathieu: To prepare the neighbourhood party,

111
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:46,640
all the neighbours pitched in.

112
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:47,880
Léa: And your quiche?

113
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:50,070
Mathieu: It smelled really good.

114
00:04:50,070 --> 00:04:53,400
I'd even tidied the kitchen before leaving.

115
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:56,520
An event rare enough to be announced.

116
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:58,200
Léa: Did your colleagues like it?

117
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:01,800
Mathieu: Yes. Then someone asked me what was in it.

118
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:04,710
I answered: mushrooms,

119
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:08,320
cheese and lots of goodwill.

120
00:05:08,320 --> 00:05:11,110
Léa: The eggs loved being forgotten.

121
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:13,600
Mathieu: I called my sister to check.

122
00:05:13,600 --> 00:05:15,460
She explained that the eggs

123
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:18,760
contributed to the dish's protein intake.

124
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,400
Léa: Protein intake.

125
00:05:20,400 --> 00:05:23,800
It's the amount of protein provided by what we eat.

126
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:25,400
Mathieu: So I can say:

127
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:28,290
chickpeas contribute to the protein

128
00:05:28,290 --> 00:05:30,720
intake of this salad.

129
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:34,330
Léa: Yes. And proteins are used in particular to build

130
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:36,880
and maintain the body's tissues.

131
00:05:36,930 --> 00:05:39,750
Mathieu: You find them in eggs, fish,

132
00:05:39,750 --> 00:05:43,560
dairy products, but also in pulses.

133
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:48,560
Léa: Exactly. Several different foods can help meet our needs.

134
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:52,080
Mathieu: My colleague had brought a white bean

135
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:55,560
salad with a few vegetables and a lemon dressing.

136
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,800
Léa: A good opportunity to talk about dietary fibre.

137
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:01,250
Mathieu: That's the part of plant foods

138
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:04,080
that our body doesn't fully digest?

139
00:06:04,130 --> 00:06:08,600
Léa: Yes. It notably helps keep digestion working well.

140
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,880
You also find it in

141
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:12,000
fruit and wholegrain cereals.

142
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:14,910
Mathieu: For example, oat flakes provide

143
00:06:14,910 --> 00:06:17,880
dietary fibre at breakfast.

144
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:18,510
Léa: That's it.

145
00:06:18,510 --> 00:06:23,160
You see, your shared lunch lets you discover several things.

146
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:26,840
Mathieu: Especially since my quiche doesn't have to work alone.

147
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:30,160
The other dishes can join its team.

148
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,640
Léa: And the vegetables your colleagues brought?

149
00:06:32,690 --> 00:06:33,460
Mathieu: Very good.

150
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:38,600
But next time, I'll write down the ingredients before leaving.

151
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:42,840
My sister would like to eat lunch without answering my survey.

152
00:06:42,840 --> 00:06:45,040
Léa: Sometimes, what makes meals complicated

153
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:47,280
is all the rules we hear.

154
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:50,800
Mathieu: Yes. One person says to cut out bread.

155
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:54,680
Another says to eat more cereals.

156
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,080
I end up getting worked up about it.

157
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:59,960
Léa: You think so much that you stress yourself out.

158
00:07:00,010 --> 00:07:02,540
Mathieu: Exactly. To choose a present,

159
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:05,840
I sometimes fret over it for days.

160
00:07:05,840 --> 00:07:07,200
Léa: With food,

161
00:07:07,200 --> 00:07:09,760
we can also be afraid of getting it wrong.

162
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:13,040
And budget or lack of time really matter.

163
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:17,800
Mathieu: Me, I thought a light dinner had to be tiny.

164
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:20,720
Once, I ate a few lettuce leaves,

165
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:23,040
then I was still hungry.

166
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:25,040
Léa: You were still hungry after the meal.

167
00:07:25,040 --> 00:07:27,680
That's the literal meaning of this expression.

168
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:29,960
Mathieu: Can you use it another way too?

169
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:34,080
Léa: Yes. The documentary was interesting, but too short.

170
00:07:34,080 --> 00:07:35,720
I was left wanting more.

171
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:40,040
Mathieu: In my case, the documentary was a salad.

172
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:42,160
Very short, indeed.

173
00:07:42,160 --> 00:07:46,160
Léa: You could have added other foods depending on your appetite.

174
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,160
Potatoes,

175
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:50,000
beans or eggs, for example.

176
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,640
Mathieu: Starchy foods, like potatoes or pasta,

177
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:56,560
provide carbohydrates in particular.

178
00:07:56,610 --> 00:07:58,720
They provide energy.

179
00:07:58,720 --> 00:08:00,920
Léa: And a varied diet also provides

180
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:04,200
different vitamins and different minerals.

181
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,960
Mathieu: So I can take an interest in what I

182
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:10,800
eat without turning every meal into an exam.

183
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:14,400
Léa: Yes, and we have different tastes and needs.

184
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:18,760
At a shared meal, everyone can find something they like.

185
00:08:18,760 --> 00:08:22,280
Mathieu: That means finding something that suits you,

186
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,600
that satisfies you.

187
00:08:23,650 --> 00:08:28,560
Léa: For example, in this library, everyone finds something for them:

188
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:33,160
novels, comics or cookbooks.

189
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:36,320
Mathieu: You already know which section to find me in!

190
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:38,280
Léa: Let's try a little scene.

191
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:40,060
I work in a café

192
00:08:40,060 --> 00:08:42,800
and you come to order your lunch.

193
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:45,880
Mathieu: You'll be able to answer before me.

194
00:08:45,880 --> 00:08:46,620
Léa: Hello!

195
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:50,100
Would you like to know what's in a dish?

196
00:08:50,150 --> 00:08:50,710
Mathieu: Your turn!

197
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:53,140
How would you ask what's

198
00:08:53,140 --> 00:08:54,920
in the salad of the day?

199
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:56,720
Take a few seconds.

200
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:00,960
Léa: You can start with "What's in…?"

201
00:09:00,960 --> 00:09:03,870
Mathieu: Hello! What's in the salad

202
00:09:03,870 --> 00:09:05,240
of the day, please?

203
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:08,170
Léa: Chickpeas, grated carrots,

204
00:09:08,170 --> 00:09:11,280
red cabbage and wholegrain semolina.

205
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:14,920
Mathieu: OK. I'm looking for something filling

206
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:17,560
because I have lunch quite early.

207
00:09:17,610 --> 00:09:20,490
Léa: Filling. It means the meal

208
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:22,960
helps satisfy your hunger.

209
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:25,290
Mathieu: For example, I find this

210
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:28,720
breakfast more filling than yesterday's.

211
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:31,600
Léa: Very good. Let's go back to our café.

212
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,960
The salad comes with bread.

213
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:36,200
Would you like the dressing on the side?

214
00:09:36,200 --> 00:09:39,240
Mathieu: Yes, thank you. What's in it?

215
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:42,150
Léa: Rapeseed oil, vinegar,

216
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:44,760
mustard and herbs.

217
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:47,390
Mathieu: Perfect. I'll have this salad

218
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:50,000
and a jug of water, please.

219
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,920
Léa: Are you eating in?

220
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:55,680
Mathieu: Yes. I have twenty minutes before going back to the office.

221
00:09:55,680 --> 00:09:57,960
Léa: Sit by the window.

222
00:09:57,960 --> 00:09:59,320
I'll bring that over.

223
00:09:59,320 --> 00:10:00,800
Mathieu: Thank you very much.

224
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:03,690
Léa: There you go. You asked about the ingredients,

225
00:10:03,690 --> 00:10:08,080
explained what you were looking for and chose your drink.

226
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:12,400
Mathieu: Without reciting a whole nutrition lecture at the till.

227
00:10:12,450 --> 00:10:17,910
Léa: You can reuse: I'm looking for something quick,

228
00:10:17,910 --> 00:10:22,480
hot, vegetarian or easy to take away.

229
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:25,340
Mathieu: And if you don't understand an ingredient,

230
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:28,200
just ask: "What's that?"

231
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:30,110
Léa: For my next market trip,

232
00:10:30,110 --> 00:10:34,720
I'm going to favour two or three easy-to-cook vegetables.

233
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:39,440
Mathieu: Favour means choosing something first?

234
00:10:39,490 --> 00:10:41,600
Léa: Yes, giving it preference.

235
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:46,040
To get around town, I prefer the tram.

236
00:10:46,040 --> 00:10:48,950
Mathieu: And I can favour recipes

237
00:10:48,950 --> 00:10:51,760
I know how to make without calling my sister.

238
00:10:51,760 --> 00:10:52,880
Léa: Very good idea.

239
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:56,680
An omelette with vegetables and bread, for example.

240
00:10:56,680 --> 00:11:00,320
Mathieu: Or pasta with peas and fish.

241
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:04,200
I can keep a few handy ingredients at home.

242
00:11:04,250 --> 00:11:07,180
Léa: Second idea: look at what we buy

243
00:11:07,180 --> 00:11:10,840
when hesitating between two similar products.

244
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,270
Mathieu: I can read the ingredients list,

245
00:11:13,270 --> 00:11:17,440
it shows what was used to make the product.

246
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,740
Léa: Yes, for example,

247
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:21,680
I checked the ingredients list of this

248
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:25,200
sauce to find out which oil it contained.

249
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:29,920
Mathieu: And the nutrition table gives amounts of nutrients.

250
00:11:29,970 --> 00:11:34,280
To compare, you need to look at the same amount of product.

251
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:37,150
Léa: The values per 100 grams, for example.

252
00:11:37,150 --> 00:11:41,200
But you can start with just one useful comparison.

253
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:45,320
Mathieu: I take two soups, I look at their salt content,

254
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:49,280
then I also choose based on my budget and my tastes.

255
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,600
Léa: Exactly.

256
00:11:50,600 --> 00:11:54,240
Third idea: keep room for what we love.

257
00:11:54,240 --> 00:11:56,880
Treating yourself matters too.

258
00:11:56,930 --> 00:12:01,640
Mathieu: Treating yourself means allowing yourself something you enjoy.

259
00:12:01,640 --> 00:12:03,320
On Saturday, I treated

260
00:12:03,320 --> 00:12:05,960
myself to a cinema ticket.

261
00:12:05,960 --> 00:12:07,100
Léa: And for meals,

262
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:11,270
a portion of dessert can be part of a varied diet.

263
00:12:11,270 --> 00:12:14,880
Frequency and amounts matter.

264
00:12:14,880 --> 00:12:17,860
Mathieu: Same principle for fats,

265
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,760
our body needs them.

266
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:23,600
Their quality and quantity are important.

267
00:12:23,650 --> 00:12:25,420
Léa: You can vary your oils,

268
00:12:25,420 --> 00:12:28,720
for example with olive or rapeseed oil,

269
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:30,760
without adding it everywhere.

270
00:12:30,760 --> 00:12:34,280
Mathieu: I'm going to try to change everything on Monday.

271
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:37,240
My shopping, my recipes, my schedule.

272
00:12:37,240 --> 00:12:40,160
Léa: Or start little by little.

273
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:43,680
Mathieu: Gradually, in small steps.

274
00:12:43,680 --> 00:12:46,660
I learned to ride a bike little by little,

275
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:48,400
in a quiet street.

276
00:12:48,450 --> 00:12:53,080
Léa: There you go, for this week, one new recipe may be enough.

277
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:55,510
And think about water during your meals.

278
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,500
Mathieu: OK, one recipe,

279
00:12:57,500 --> 00:13:01,490
one jug and no big speech to my saucepans.

280
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:06,710
Léa: Now, tell us about your dish from the start.

281
00:13:06,770 --> 00:13:08,870
Here's a simple structure.

282
00:13:08,870 --> 00:13:12,420
I often make…, there's…,

283
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:14,570
I like this dish because…

284
00:13:14,570 --> 00:13:17,890
Mathieu: I often make a mushroom quiche.

285
00:13:17,890 --> 00:13:20,280
There are eggs, milk,

286
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:24,020
mushrooms and a bit of cheese.

287
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:25,780
I like this dish because I

288
00:13:25,780 --> 00:13:28,450
can share it with my colleagues.

289
00:13:28,450 --> 00:13:31,510
Léa: I often make a vegetable soup.

290
00:13:31,510 --> 00:13:33,080
There are carrots,

291
00:13:33,080 --> 00:13:36,170
leeks and potatoes.

292
00:13:36,170 --> 00:13:38,510
I like this dish because it warms me up

293
00:13:38,510 --> 00:13:41,150
and I can keep some for the next day.

294
00:13:41,150 --> 00:13:44,870
Mathieu: Your turn, say your sentence out loud.

295
00:13:44,870 --> 00:13:47,310
Even three very simple sentences,

296
00:13:47,310 --> 00:13:50,670
that's already a conversation starting.

297
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:52,600
Léa: You can add…

298
00:13:52,650 --> 00:13:55,050
This week, I'm going to…

299
00:13:55,050 --> 00:13:57,710
Then choose a small change.

300
00:13:57,710 --> 00:14:00,620
Mathieu: This week, I'm going to write down the ingredients

301
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:03,770
of my recipe before the shared lunch.

302
00:14:03,770 --> 00:14:06,030
Léa: Me, I'm going to check my schedule

303
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:08,830
before filling my basket.

304
00:14:08,830 --> 00:14:13,430
Mathieu: You can reuse our structure with your own foods.

305
00:14:13,430 --> 00:14:16,970
The name of a dish from your country is perfect.

306
00:14:16,970 --> 00:14:20,040
Léa: Let's go back over five expressions.

307
00:14:20,090 --> 00:14:24,410
Listen, then repeat calmly with us.

308
00:14:24,410 --> 00:14:26,730
Mathieu: First, at the market,

309
00:14:26,730 --> 00:14:30,390
Léa's eyes were bigger than her stomach.

310
00:14:30,390 --> 00:14:33,530
She'd bought too much food.

311
00:14:33,530 --> 00:14:38,170
Léa: It's wanting to eat more than you really can.

312
00:14:38,170 --> 00:14:41,950
New example. I ordered two desserts, but

313
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:44,210
I didn't finish the first one.

314
00:14:44,210 --> 00:14:47,220
Mathieu: Your eyes were bigger than your stomach.

315
00:14:47,270 --> 00:14:51,890
Let's repeat: avoir les yeux plus gros que le ventre.

316
00:14:51,890 --> 00:14:54,010
Léa: Next, you got your hands

317
00:14:54,010 --> 00:14:56,970
dirty making the quiche.

318
00:14:56,970 --> 00:15:00,090
Mathieu: Yes, I took part in the work.

319
00:15:00,090 --> 00:15:03,250
You can use this expression in cooking

320
00:15:03,250 --> 00:15:05,970
but also for helping with a project.

321
00:15:05,970 --> 00:15:08,110
Léa: Before the shop opened,

322
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:10,090
the whole family pitched

323
00:15:10,090 --> 00:15:13,080
in to put up the shelves.

324
00:15:13,130 --> 00:15:17,070
Mathieu: Let's repeat: mettre la main à la pâte.

325
00:15:17,070 --> 00:15:20,910
Léa: Third expression: se prendre la tête.

326
00:15:20,910 --> 00:15:22,940
We used it to talk about

327
00:15:22,940 --> 00:15:25,830
the food rules that stress us out.

328
00:15:25,830 --> 00:15:30,070
Mathieu: It's overcomplicating things or worrying too much.

329
00:15:30,070 --> 00:15:33,830
Example: don't stress about the decorations,

330
00:15:33,830 --> 00:15:35,890
a few flowers will do.

331
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:39,820
Léa: Let's repeat: se prendre la tête.

332
00:15:39,870 --> 00:15:42,850
This expression is informal and common

333
00:15:42,850 --> 00:15:45,170
in a conversation between friends.

334
00:15:45,170 --> 00:15:49,130
Mathieu: Fourth expression: rester sur sa faim.

335
00:15:49,130 --> 00:15:52,610
After my little salad, I was still hungry.

336
00:15:52,610 --> 00:15:57,170
Léa: Figuratively, you expected more from something.

337
00:15:57,170 --> 00:16:00,330
Example: the tour ended too quickly,

338
00:16:00,330 --> 00:16:02,570
we were left wanting more.

339
00:16:02,570 --> 00:16:05,840
Mathieu: Let's repeat: rester sur sa faim.

340
00:16:05,890 --> 00:16:10,130
This time, nobody's asking for a second lunch.

341
00:16:10,130 --> 00:16:12,970
Léa: And finally, trouver son compte.

342
00:16:12,970 --> 00:16:16,730
Everyone finds something that meets their expectations.

343
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:21,850
Mathieu: Example: on that holiday, everyone found something they liked.

344
00:16:21,850 --> 00:16:23,350
My sister went cycling

345
00:16:23,350 --> 00:16:26,530
and I discovered the restaurants.

346
00:16:26,530 --> 00:16:29,860
Léa: Let's repeat: trouver son compte.

347
00:16:29,910 --> 00:16:32,250
Now choose one of these

348
00:16:32,250 --> 00:16:36,010
expressions and imagine another situation.

349
00:16:36,010 --> 00:16:39,170
Mathieu: Your example can be about food,

350
00:16:39,170 --> 00:16:41,210
work or an outing.

351
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:44,410
The main thing is that it's like you.

352
00:16:44,410 --> 00:16:46,510
Léa: For your comment,

353
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:52,850
write: I often make… because… This week I'm going to…

354
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:56,780
Mathieu: You can also ask a question about an ingredient.

355
00:16:56,830 --> 00:17:00,010
We love discovering what people cook where you live.

356
00:17:00,010 --> 00:17:02,140
Léa: And if this episode helped you,

357
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:03,930
subscribe to The Cozy French

358
00:17:03,930 --> 00:17:06,810
to keep practising with us.

359
00:17:06,810 --> 00:17:11,690
Mathieu: Listen again to a short exchange and repeat both roles.

360
00:17:11,690 --> 00:17:15,090
You can start with the order at the café.

361
00:17:15,090 --> 00:17:18,090
Léa: Thank you for sharing this break with us.

362
00:17:18,090 --> 00:17:20,810
Take care and see you very soon!

363
00:17:20,810 --> 00:17:22,810
Mathieu: Goodbye everyone!

364
00:17:22,810 --> 00:17:26,140
I just have one thing left to sort out.

365
00:17:26,190 --> 00:17:28,010
Léa: Your quiche's CV?

366
00:17:28,010 --> 00:17:31,170
Mathieu: Yes. In the references section,

367
00:17:31,170 --> 00:17:33,050
should I put my sister's number?

368
00:17:33,050 --> 00:17:34,640
Léa: Put the recipe instead,

369
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:38,890
it finally deserves a quiet lunch break.
